       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. TCCSFTPCHK.
       AUTHOR.     JEFF BUNGO.
       INSTALLATION.  GOODYEAR TIRE & RUBBER CO.
       DATE-WRITTEN.   09/23/97.
       DATE-COMPILED.  XX/XX/XX.
      *************************************************************
      *  THIS PROGRAM IS CHECK THE OUTPUT GENERATED FROM THE      *
      *  FTP COMMANDS IN BATCH MODE.                              *
      *                                                           *
      *  ERROR CODES ARE DOCUMENTED IN THE AS/400 TCP/IP USERS    *
      *  GUIDE.                                                   *
      *                                                           *
      *  THIS PROGRAM WILL MONITOR FOR ANY 4XX OR 5XX MESSAGES    *
      *  WHICH WILL INDICATE AN ERROR OCCURRED DURING THE FILE    *
      *  TRANSFER ROUTINE. IF AN ERROR IS FOUND, THE RETURN       *
      *  PARAMETER WILL BE SET TO '1'.                            *
      *                                                           *
      *************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-AS400.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.   REQUESTOR IS WORK-STATION
                        SYSTEM-CONSOLE IS CONSOLE
                        SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN IS SHUTDOWN-SWITCH
                               ON STATUS IS SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN-REQUESTED
                        LOCAL-DATA IS LOCAL-DATA-AREA.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
            SELECT QTXTSRC-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-QTXTSRC
                   ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                   ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
                   RECORD KEY IS SRCSEQ
                   FILE STATUS IS QTXTSRC-SK.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  QTXTSRC-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  QTXTSRC-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF QTXTSRC.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  FTP-FLAG                            PIC X.
       01  FILE-STATUS-KEYS.
           03  QTXTSRC-SK                      PIC X(2)  VALUE ZERO.
       01  SWITCHES.
           03  SW-ON                           PIC 1 VALUE B"1".
           03  SW-OFF                          PIC 1 VALUE B"0".
       01  SRCDTA-XX.
           05  RETURN-CODE-XX.
               10  RC-1-XX                     PIC X.
               10  RC-23-XX                    PIC X(2).
           05  RC-SPACE                        PIC X.
           05  RC-MESSAGE                      PIC X(76).
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01  FLAG-PARM                           PIC X.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING FLAG-PARM.
       000-OPEN.
           OPEN INPUT  QTXTSRC-FILE.
       010-MAIN.
           PERFORM 020-INIT                    THRU 020-EXIT.
           PERFORM 100-PROCESS                 THRU 100-EXIT.
           PERFORM 900-CLOSE-FILES             THRU 900-EXIT.
       010-EOJ.
           EXIT PROGRAM.
       RPG-CL-EXIT.
           STOP RUN.

       020-INIT.
           MOVE '0'                            TO FTP-FLAG.
       020-EXIT.
           EXIT.
      /
       100-PROCESS.
           PERFORM READ-QTXTSRC.
           PERFORM 110-READ-FILE               THRU 110-EXIT UNTIL
               FTP-FLAG   NOT EQUAL ZERO OR
               QTXTSRC-SK NOT EQUAL ZERO.
           MOVE FTP-FLAG                       TO FLAG-PARM.
       100-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       110-READ-FILE.
           MOVE SRCDTA                         TO SRCDTA-XX.
           IF SRCDTA-XX (1:8) EQUAL 'Not able'
               MOVE '1'                        TO FTP-FLAG.
           IF RETURN-CODE-XX EQUAL '425' OR '426' OR '450' OR '451' OR
                                   '452' OR
                                   '500' OR '501' OR '502' OR '503' OR
                                   '504' OR '530' OR '532' OR '550' OR
                                   '551' OR '552' OR '553'
               IF RC-SPACE EQUAL SPACE
                   IF RC-MESSAGE (1:5) NOT EQUAL 'bytes'
                        MOVE '1'                TO FTP-FLAG.
           PERFORM READ-QTXTSRC.
       110-EXIT.
           EXIT.
      /
       READ-QTXTSRC.
           READ QTXTSRC-FILE RECORD.

       900-CLOSE-FILES.
           CLOSE QTXTSRC-FILE.
       900-EXIT.
           EXIT.
